    "bottomLine": "The folding USB panel to buy if you want the most margin for clouds, short days and a power bank that needs filling.",
    "description": "BigBlue’s 28W charger has been one of the default answers for a solar powered cell phone charger for years, and for a simple reason: it has more panel area than the 21W crowd, so it has more headroom when the sun is not cooperating. BigBlue lists SunPower cells and three USB-A ports. Like every USB panel, it will not deliver its full rating through a phone cable; the panel is rated at the cells under ideal lab light, and real output after heat, angle and the 5V regulator is commonly about half to two-thirds of that. That still makes it the best tool here for filling a 10,000-20,000mAh bank during a long sunny day, which is the job that matters. Hang it facing the sun, plug a bank into it rather than your phone, and charge the phone from the bank in the evening. If you need USB-C Power Delivery for a laptop, this is the wrong product; look at a power station instead."
  },
  {
    "id": "anker-powerport-solar-21w",
    "name": "Anker PowerPort Solar 21W Solar Charger",
    "category": "21W folding USB panel, 2 USB-A ports",
    "badge": "Best Lightweight Folding Panel",
    "amazonUrl": "",
