    "bottomLine": "The battery half of the best solar setup: pair it with any 21W-28W folding panel.",
    "description": "This is the product that makes a folding panel useful. The Anker 335 is a plain 20,000mAh power bank with USB-C and USB-A, and it has no solar cell at all, which is exactly the point. Paired with a 21W or 28W folding panel, it soaks up the midday harvest while you hike or sit out an outage, then charges your phone at full speed at night, from a cable, without the stop-start behavior of charging a phone straight from a panel. At roughly 74Wh nominal, a full bank holds about three to four charges for most current phones once conversion losses are counted, which is a long weekend of normal use or several days of careful outage use. Filling it from empty takes a full sunny day on a 28W panel, so in practice you top it up a third or half at a time. If you need to charge a laptop, step up to a USB-C PD bank instead."
