            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "They work as power banks, and the solar part works only as a slow trickle. A built-in cell produces roughly a watt or two in ideal sun, so filling a 10,000mAh bank from solar alone takes days of direct light. For real solar charging, pair a separate 21-28W folding panel with a plain power bank and charge the bank during the day."
