          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it safe to leave a solar power bank in a hot car?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It is not a good idea. Lithium batteries age faster when hot, and a dashboard in summer sun can get far hotter than battery makers recommend. That is one of the strongest arguments for a folding panel, which can sit in the sun while the battery stays in the shade at the end of a cable."
          }
        },
